The range for $x$, given the constraints, is $x \in \left[ -\frac{1}{2}, \frac{7}{8} \right).$  To find the values of $\lfloor \lfloor 2x \rfloor - \frac{1}{2} \rfloor,$ write $2x$ as $m + f,$ where $m \in \mathbb{Z},$ and $0 \le f < 1.$  The expression therefore simplifies to $\lfloor m + f - \frac{1}{2} \rfloor.$

It is useful to break the range of $x$ into several sub-ranges.  To be given by $x \ge -\frac{1}{2},$ we only need $0 \le x + 2 < 3.$  On the interval $\left[ -\frac{1}{2}, \frac{7}{8} \right),$ we have $x + 2 \in \left[ \frac{3}{8}, \frac{23}{8} \right).$  Then, as $0 \le x + 2 < 3,$ the second part is always the integer.  Similarly, as $0 \le x + 2 < 3,$ $\lfloor x + 2 \rfloor = [x + 2] = m,$ and we have both ranges of $x$ where we have $m = 1.$ [asy]
